    "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution to a Trigonometric Equation Containing Tangent or Cotangent",
    "problem": "Find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}.$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
    "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\n$$",
